This photo shows leftovers after a meal: a brown sauce residue on the large plate, small cups with traces of condiments, a pink item (possibly ham or salmon) in one cup, and a glass with a little liquid. Very little food remains.

I estimated the residue at about 15 g of sauce, 5 g of the pink item, and a few grams of other traces. That comes to roughly 25 g of food in total. At about 1.5 kcal per gram for sauces mixed with fats, the total is around 40 kcal.

